            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of leukotriene receptor antagonist on cough variant asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>694-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To study the curative effect of leukotriene receptor antagonist on cough variant asthma (CVA).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Sixty-four CVA patients received treatment with bricany and montelukas and 68 control patients had bricany treatment for 4 weeks. The recurrence rate was observed in the two groups during the follow-up for 6 months.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The remission time of two groups were 2.5-/+3.6 and 5.3-/+3.8 days in acute phase, respectively, showing a significant difference between them (P&lt;0.05). The recurrence rate of the two groups within 6 months were 20.09% and 40.87%, respectively, showing also significantly differences (P&lt;0.05).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Leukotriene receptor antagonist and bricany can effectively control CVA and significantly lower the short-term recurrence rate of CVA.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
